.SH MEMORY AND CRAFT
.TP
.B lk memory
Show the durable summary and bounded candidate memories with importance values.
.TP
.B lk memory add TEXT [--importance N]
Add a compact user memory. Importance defaults to 60 and is clamped to 1 through 100.
.TP
.B lk memory forget TEXT
Remove candidate memories containing TEXT.
.TP
.B lk forget TEXT
Short form of memory forget.
.TP
.B lk memory clear
Clear this user's LO memory after confirmation.
.TP
.B lk memory clear-summary
Clear only the long-term summary while preserving candidate memories.
.TP
.B lk memory prune
Remove known reasoning/meta artifacts from persisted memory.
.TP
.B lk clear-memory
Short form of memory clear.
.TP
.B lk skills
Show LO's reusable bundled and locally learned assistant craft.
.TP
.B lk skills add TEXT
Manually add one generalized reusable lesson to the Learned section.
.TP
.B lk skills forget TEXT
Remove matching locally learned skills.
.TP
.B lk skills clear-learned
Clear locally learned skills while preserving bundled release craft.
.TP
.B lk skills path
Print the editable skills file path.
.PP
Automatic skill learning is enabled in workspace, power, and unsafe profiles and disabled in conservative.
.PP
LO keeps at most 20 candidate memories on disk and offers at most eight to immediate prompt attention.
Unused memories decay during maintenance. Retrieval by itself does not reinforce a memory.
User memory and reusable assistant skills are deliberately separate.
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
.B lk settings
Unified interactive panel for access profile, machine-local preferred model, Fabric routing, legacy direct Ollama host/model, web-search key, and Ollama tailnet share.
It uses the same underlying state and commands; it is not a second configuration system.
