.TP
.B lmk FILE.ext
Create an empty file through LOOK's undo journal.
.TP
.B lmk DIR/
Create a directory and enter it. The creation is journaled for
.B lk undo
.
.TP
.B lmk -f NAME
Force file creation when the name is ambiguous.
.TP
.B lmk -d NAME
Force directory creation and enter it.
.TP
.B mkd DIR
Compatibility wrapper for
.B lmk -d DIR
.
.PP
A trailing slash is directory intent. Names with a filename suffix and dotfiles imply file intent.
Extensionless names are prompted as directory or file. The choice is accepted immediately from a single key; Return is not required.
Missing parent directories for file creation require confirmation.
Undo removes only an unchanged empty created file or an empty created directory.
.SH INTERACTIVE LOOK KEYS
Arrow keys move the selection. Selection itself enters object inspection/preview state.
Shift-arrow navigation provides fast top/page/bottom movement.
Tab marks or unmarks objects. C opens Copy To; M opens Move To.
Shift-D removes the selected or marked set after confirmation.
Shift-R renames the selected or marked set; #, ##, and ### in a batch pattern expand to 1, 01, and 001 style numbering.
In rename editing, Left/Right move the caret, Home/End jump, Backspace/Delete edit, Enter commits, and Esc alone cancels.
.PP
Copy To and Move To keep the editable destination line canonical. Tab completes paths; Down/Right opens the directory picker; Left moves to the parent; Right descends; Enter accepts the displayed destination; Esc cancels.

