.SH CAPABILITY MODEL
Remote inference and local authority are separate:
.B lo @HOST --power
runs inference on HOST while commands execute on the computer running LOOK.
Thinking-capable output is visually separated into
.B thinking >
and
.B lo >
sections; tool activity remains distinct.
.SH FABRIC VISION
.TP
.B lk vision screen [@NODE]
Capture one desktop frame from the local node or a trusted Fabric peer. The endpoint uses a temporary capture file only for the duration of the request; no screenshot history is maintained.
.TP
.B lk vision screen @NODE --ask QUESTION
Capture one frame and pass it directly to the selected local vision model. The screenshot is not persisted.
.TP
.B lk vision screen @NODE --save FILE
Explicitly persist the received frame at FILE.
.TP
.B lk vision screen @NODE --watch [DURATION] --every INTERVAL
Run an explicit foreground observation session. Duration is bounded to ten minutes, interval to at least two seconds, Ctrl-C stops immediately, and unchanged hashes return metadata without retransmitting image bytes.
.TP
.B Security
Remote screen capture uses normal authenticated Fabric peer transport. The Unified Node contains no autonomous capture scheduler.
