.SH COMPLETION
LOOK installs context-sensitive Zsh completion for
.B lk
and
.B lo
under ~/.config/look/completions.
Commands such as
.B lk ollama
,
.B lk memory
, and
.B lk skills
complete their valid subcommands. The
.B lmk
completion exposes file/directory force flags and existing parent directories.
Saved Ollama host names are completed dynamically.
LO completion stops at its command/options layer so free-form prompt text remains free-form.
.SH VERSION SAFETY
Future Crash + LOOK installers write a versioned install manifest under
~/.local/share/look/install_manifest.json.
A current installer refuses to overwrite a newer unified release unless
.B --force-downgrade
is supplied deliberately.
Historical installers predating this guard cannot be retroactively protected.

.SH MEDIA
.TP
.B lk mp [QUERY]
Open the integrated LOOK Media Player: Fabric library search, remote/local artwork, queue, now-playing state, and transport controls in one terminal surface.
.TP
.B lk player
Open the live LOOK terminal miniplayer for the current MediaSession. It shares Media Find's Chafa terminal-art renderer, shows playback/EQ state, and closing it does not stop playback.
.TP
.B lk scan [ROOT]
Build or refresh the lightweight ordinary-file metadata catalog. With no ROOT, scan the user home with conservative cache/build/hidden-directory exclusions. File contents are not read or hashed.
.TP
.B lk catalog
Show local file-catalog coverage and indexed roots.
.TP
.B lk find QUERY
Search cataloged filenames and paths using lightweight natural-language metadata terms. Uses the reachable Fabric union when available and falls back to the local catalog offline.
.TP
.B lk media
Show the current LOOK media session, state, track, progress, and queue position.
.TP
.B lk media scan ROOT
Build or refresh the fast dependency-free media library index for ROOT. Media bytes are not hashed or decoded during the scan.
.TP
.B lk media play TARGET [--shuffle] [--exact]
Play a file, directory, selector, or indexed artist/album/title query as a LOOK-owned queue. Ordinary names use forgiving fuzzy matching; --exact (or --literal) requests deterministic literal lookup.
.TP
.B lk media queue
Show the canonical queue around the current item.
.TP
.B lk media browse [QUERY]
Open the LOOK-native Fabric media selector. Type to filter immediately, Tab multi-selects, Enter/P plays, Q queues, A queues visible matches, and exact display-name retyping is unnecessary.
.TP
.B lk media find QUERY
Search the online Fabric media catalog and open the same selector when interactive. Local embedded/sidecar cover art renders in terminal form when available. Fabric currently transports media identity/location, not a separate remote cover-art asset.
.TP
.B lk media fabric
Show the union of scanned media on currently reachable Fabric nodes, including per-node scanned and SHA-identified counts.

.TP
.B lk media outputs
List reachable Fabric playback endpoints. Each node owns its local player/output session.

.TP
.B lk media on NODE play TARGET
Start TARGET on NODE rather than the current machine. Transport forms include toggle, next, prev, stop, and state.
.TP
.B lk media identify QUERY|PATH|--all
Promote discovered media to SHA-256 Fabric artifact identity. Bulk --all is deliberately local to the current node.
.TP
.B lk media save NAME
Save the current queue as a persistent playlist.
.TP
.B lk media load NAME
Restore and play a saved playlist.
.TP
.B lk media playlists
List saved playlists.
.TP
.B lk media repeat [off|all]
Set or toggle repeat-all for the current queue.
.TP
.B lk media stream PATH
Explicitly register PATH as a Fabric artifact and play its byte-range stream. Remote content-addressed form: lk media stream @NODE sha256:DIGEST.
.TP
.B lk media toggle / next / prev / stop
Control the LOOK-owned media session. When no LOOK session exists, supported system-player control remains available.
.TP
.B lk media state
Print a compact JSON snapshot of the canonical LOOK media session for renderer/control surfaces.
.TP
.B lk media jump INDEX
Jump deterministically to the one-based queue item INDEX in the current LOOK media session.
.PP
mpv is the standard LOOK playback edge and is installed as part of the workstation dependency set. LOOK owns queue/session meaning; mpv owns decoding and rendering. Same-node queues may use direct local file access, while remote/content-addressed entries use Fabric artifact streams.

.SH FABRIC IDENTITY, ENDPOINTS, AND TRANSPORT
.TP
.B lk fabric identity
Show the stable Fabric node identity and fingerprint.
.TP
.B lk fabric pair-code
Open a five-minute, one-use node pairing invitation.
.TP
.B lk fabric pair NODE CODE
Pair with a reachable node using the short numeric invitation code. Pairing mints reciprocal Fabric authorization credentials.
.TP
.B lk fabric transport
Show Tailcat direct-TLS endpoints and the active route to reachable peers. Tailcat is preferred when directly reachable; Tailscale is retained as fallback/bootstrap transport.
.TP
.B lk fabric endpoints
Aggregate pending, temporary, and trusted browser endpoints across reachable trusted nodes.
.TP
.B lk fabric allow CODE once|trust
Approve a browser authorization request on whichever reachable Fabric node owns that pending code.
.TP
.B lk fabric revoke-endpoint ENDPOINT_ID
Revoke the endpoint on the Fabric node that owns it.
.PP
Tailcat phase 1 listens on TCP 7443 with a node-local TLS certificate pinned through Fabric trust. It does not yet provide NAT traversal, relays, or browser exposure; those remain separate reachability layers.

