.SH SELECTED PATHS TO LO
In the interactive filer FILTER or SELECT view, press
.B L
to launch LO with the current marked paths as explicit context.
If no paths are marked, the highlighted path is used.
The files are not bulk-loaded into the model context; LO receives a path manifest and reads only what it needs through its bounded file tools.

.SH FILER NAVIGATION
Use
.B j
and
.B k
(or uppercase J/K) and the up/down arrow keys for vertical movement.
.B L
is reserved for the selected-path LO context handoff.

.SH FILESYSTEM PARENT
In the plain filer browse state, press
.B <
(Shift-comma)
to move to the real filesystem parent directory.
This is distinct from Escape, which navigates LOOK history.
While entering a filter, < is treated as ordinary filter text.

.SH PERSISTENT WORKING SET
Selections persist across filer directory navigation.
Use Tab to toggle one item, A to toggle current matches, and X to clear the set.
When the set spans locations, the status reports the total and the number visible here as
.B SELECTED \(bu N / H HERE.
Copy, move, remove, path-copy, clipboard, and LO-context actions use the persistent set when non-empty.

.SH PATH COMPLETION
LOOK copy and move destination prompts support Tab completion for filesystem paths.
The lcp, lmv, lrm, and lscp helpers use normal repeated Zsh path completion for each operand.
.SH GLOBAL FIND
.B f
performs a LOOK-native global find rooted at the user's home directory.
.B fznv
uses the same finder and opens the selected file in Neovim.
.SH TEMPORAL MEMORY
Recent exchanges and semantic memory candidates carry age information.
Memory is historical context and must not be treated as pending work.
.SH BACKGROUND LO
.B lo bg REQUEST
queues one-shot LO work in the background.
Completed or failed jobs produce durable LOOK events, surfaced automatically at a subsequent Zsh prompt.
Use
.B lk jobs
and
.B lk events
to inspect state.

.SH PROFILE
.B lk profile
shows the portable LOOK identity.
.B lk profile backup [DEST]
creates rotating timestamped backups and remembers DEST.
.B lk profile export [ZIP]
creates a migration archive.
.B lk profile restore SOURCE
restores a profile after schema/path validation and creates a local safety snapshot first.
Secrets and runtime state are excluded.
.SH FEEDBACK
.B lk feedback
configures finite terminal motion and optional sound.
.B lk sound
toggles sound.
Sound defaults off; motion defaults subtle; non-TTY output is silent and static.
.SH SKILLS EXPORT
.B lk skills export [FILE]
writes only locally learned skills for review or promotion into a future distribution.
\n.SH LIVING AI\n.B lk ai\nopens the AI control surface.\n.B lk ai status\nshows the resident broker, foreground state, and queue depths.\n.B lk ai start\nstarts the local broker;\n.B lk ai stop\nstops it. The broker coordinates durable background jobs, memory consolidation, and skill reflection while interactive LO work has foreground priority.\n